# P2 independent review brief

Review P2 against the campaign-admission spec and P2 plan, including the accepted principal clarifications below. This task adds only immutable live admission facts and native pre-persistence/pre-reservation guards. P3 enrollment/operation stopping and P4 completed-history integration are intentionally absent. Source must be frozen before review; use the implementer's exact final hashes and unified diff against the three actual byte preimages in `principal-preimages/authority.json`.

Allowed production diff: additions to `campaign_admission.py`, one factory helper and its three guarded complete-request return sites plus necessary imports in `production_runtime.py`, and the policy branch within `production_provider.py:LocalRoleAuthorizationLedgerV5.reserve_role_slot` plus imports. All other existing definitions and every old serialized shape/identity formula remain unchanged. The approved P1 source begins at SHA `7e15ed500121b4c85df7a838feab51750e1f476a3e5427b9d1a0b1f0f58a89d9`; both its finite-USD corrections and exact fixed-output requirement must survive.

Named risks to check against actual diff and focused unchanged dependencies:

1. Normal factory guard returns only after checking current enrollment, actual input round and owner, authenticated original launch/config/start/root/deadlines and exact prospective envelope. There are exactly three guarded request-return sites, before runtime `_complete_role` persists anything. No policy state is cached in a constructor; absence remains legacy.
2. Ledger guard runs under the existing transition, before reservation construction/append, retaining original duplicate/incomplete checks and budget/accounting order. The old content-only request lookup and original time acquisition remain on the legacy path. Resolve exact persisted call/request only for enrollment; do not globally tighten legacy duplicate-identical-content behavior.
3. `RoleRequestV5` has no round field. Factory supplies actual inputs; ledger derives context from `load_unique_role_request_entry_by_sha256` and verifies campaign, round, role position, primary attempt/index and exact request SHA. Optional caller owner is checked only when supplied after enrollment discovery; the ledger authenticates the original durable owner independently.
4. Selected state census covers both value/index halves. A selected round under a wrong key must not disappear merely because its key differs from the selected canonical hash. Use owner/config/manifest linkage to distinguish selected orphan state from authenticated foreign state. Reject gaps, unsupported later state, mismatches and out-of-range state.
5. Prior-round eligibility requires authentic settled contiguous rounds, committed records with critic binding and successful cleanup, and actual verified paid prefix usage. All actual prior journal packages and earlier current roles remain bound to ordered ledger receipts. Do not force a partial repository through whole completed-history census or a wrapper/filter.
6. At factory time the current actual request may be absent; at ledger time it is persisted. Only the exact current request/call may be the one unjournaled tail, with its matching pending/terminal ledger tail when normal recovery requires it. Reject arbitrary orphans, multiple current primary calls, skipped roles, failed-predecessor continuation and later calls hidden by prefix slicing. Native duplicate/incomplete refusal still prevents replay from reserving again.
7. Authentic already-completed request replay may remain read-only. A settled current round cannot admit a new role/call. Current author/critic continuation uses the original prior-round admission counters and does not reserve another three-call round after its own earlier roles spent budget.
8. Historical/shared facts use only immutable readers: all typed-state and projection reads explicitly `repair=False`; no live ledger/gateway/executor, recovery/migration, clock/nonce or provider construction. Read-only H1/H2 workspace/mount history constructors remain the accepted existing boundary. Real-now checks belong to the live guard, not a substituted historical clock. Local imports must avoid the existing module cycles.

Verification limits: no tests may be read, created, modified or run; no synthetic/fake cases, artifacts, probes, source imports to execute, credentials/environment values, provider/API/Docker/evaluator/campaign activity or actual summary calls. Review source/AST/diff/hash and reported scoped Ruff/in-memory compile only. Do not require or invent dynamic coverage. Preserve all 579 runtime-04 and 83 provider-runtime-06 files plus the 56-file evaluator map `005064e57e80840f3b2a97d7db694b176832b8f982996e63efc8a35064505ed4`.

Report spec compliance and quality separately, with actionable prioritized findings and precise evidence. No source edits or subagents. Final review report lives in this P2 evidence directory; after fixes use the actual retained preimage and narrow fix diff, never claim a hash alone is retained source bytes.
